  "required_semantics": {
    "reset": "Clear both valid bits and suppress accept/move/response; payload clearing is not claimed.",
    "flush": "Blocks all new accepts; surviving P may move and surviving R may respond.",
    "partial_cancel": "Each slot uses its own ROB pointer. Unrelated flush does not cancel the slot.",
    "backpressure": "When liveR && !out.ready, move is blocked; a live P also blocks new acceptance. If P is not live, it may accept when input/admission/reset/flush conditions permit.",
